A beginner Java programming project simulating a medieval blacksmith shop to show knowledge of abstract data types.

## Features
- Creates equipment objects.
- Stores equipment names, weights, and values.
- Calculates total inventory weight and value.
- Identifies valuable equipment worth 200 gold or more.

## Concepts Demonstrated
- Abstract Data Types (ADTs)
- Encapsulation
- Constructors
- Getter methods
- Boolean methods
- Object creation and interaction

## Language and IDE
- Java
- Eclipse
